Fishing uses different type of tools, each of which is used at different fishing spots to catch different types of fish. Unlike [[pickaxes]] for mining or [[hatchets]] for woodcutting, higher level fishing tools do not typically come with increases to the rate of catching fish, but instead they grant access to new fishing methods.

===Nets===
[[File:Fishing with Net.gif|thumb|A player fishing with a small net.]]
The first few fish players can catch require nets, which are mostly used in the seas. Free players can only use [[small fishing net]]s, while members can also use [[big fishing net]]s. The big net allows players to catch higher-level fish such as [[raw seerfish|seerfish]] and [[raw sillago|sillago]], and items such as [[caskets]].

The [[small cast net]] and [[big cast net]] are unlocked at higher levels and are wieldable versions of the small and big nets, saving inventory space, but otherwise function identically.

===Rods===
[[Fishing rod]]s for bait fishing can be used in both rivers and seas, and are used to catch a veriety of fish, from [[raw sardine|sardines]] (level 5) to [[raw sailfish|sailfish]] (level 97). Along with the rod, players need [[fishing bait]] to attract fish, with each fish caught using up one bait.

[[Fly fishing rod]]s for lure fishing are required for certain mid-level fish caught in rivers. Instead of fishing bait, players will need [[feathers]] to attract fish such as [[raw trout|trout]] (level 20) and [[raw salmon|salmon]] (level 30). Each fish caught uses one feather. Feathers can be bought on the [[Grand Exchange]] for {{NoCoins|{{GEPrice|Feather}}|c}} each, or bought from [[fishing shops]] for {{NoCoins|6|c}} each.

Another rod is the [[barbarian rod]], which is used to catch leaping trout, leaping salmon, and leaping sturgeon, during and after [[Barbarian Fishing]].

The [[crystal fishing rod]] is a high level rod which functions as all 3 other types of rod; standard, fly, and barbarian.

===Cages===
[[Crayfish cage|Crayfish cages]] are a very early level fishing method used to catch [[Raw crayfish|crayfish]], which are found in rivers and lakes.

[[Lobster pot|Lobster pots]] are a mid-level fishing method used to catch [[Raw lobster|lobsters]], which are are found in the sea. Lobster is recommended for fishing levels 60 to 99 for non-members, though they take a bit longer to catch than other fish. A popular cage spot is in Karamja due to [[Stiles]]'s presence, who changes tuna, swordfish or lobster into [[note]]s, allowing players to fish indefinitely without depositing items at a bank. An alternative would be to use the Port Sarim lodestone, Entrana deposit box, then return via ship to Musa Point; the entire trip takes fewer clicks, and less time, than a trip to see Stiles.

===Harpoons===
{{Main|Harpoons}}
Harpoons are required for catching some larger medium to high level fish: mainly [[Raw tuna|tuna]], [[Raw swordfish|swordfish]] and [[Raw shark|sharks]]. They can only be used in the sea. When a player has found a fishing spot, they can then use their harpoon if the "Harpoon" option is available.

There are four types of harpoons - the (regular) [[harpoon]], the [[barb-tail harpoon]], the [[sacred clay harpoon]], and the [[dragon harpoon]]. All harpoons other than the regular harpoon can be equipped in the main hand and have various bonuses over using the regular harpoon, however the regular harpoon is the only one that can be added to the [[tool belt]].

Members can speak with [[Otto Godblessed]] in his [[Otto's Grotto|home]] near [[Baxtorian Falls]] to learn [[Barbarian Fishing]], which allows players to fish tuna, swordfish, and sharks without a harpoon. Using this barehanded method requires a higher Fishing level as well as a Strength level equivalent to the Fishing level needed to catch the fish normally.

===Quest tools===
The [[oily fishing rod]] is a special kind of fishing rod involved in the [[Heroes' Quest]], however it may be used after the quest to fish [[lava eel]]s in the [[Taverly dungeon]].

The [[karambwan vessel]] is a unique pot involved in the [[Tai Bwo Wannai Trio]] quest, however it may be used after the quest to fish [[karambwan]]s on [[Karamja]]. Fishing karambwan requires [[karambwanji]] as bait.

===Rod-o-matics===
The [[fishing rod-o-matic]] and [[enhanced fishing rod-o-matic]] are invention [[devices]] that can be used in place of all other standard fishing tools (not including quest-related tools) and allow for fishing at any standard fishing spot. They can accept [[tool gizmo]]s and [[ancient tool gizmo]] to have [[tool perk]]s, however using them costs [[charge pack|divine charge]] for every fishing action performed.

==Fishing spots==
{{main|Fishing spot}}

There are four main types of fishing spots in ''RuneScape'', listed below. The type of fishing spot determines the equipment needed and the kinds of fish the player will catch; for example, [[raw salmon]] can only be caught using a [[fly fishing rod]] at combination [[Fishing spot (lure, bait)|lure/bait fishing spots]].

Make sure to pay attention to both right-click options, as the equipment needed may differ between locations with an option of the same name. For example, if attempting to net fish, fishing spots require a [[small fishing net]] when the options are "Net" and "Bait", but require a [[big fishing net]] if the options are "Net" and "Harpoon" instead.

Other fishing spots that are locked behind quests or activities, occur in few locations, only produce a single type of fish, or have other additional requirements are listed in the [[fishing spot]] article.

{{List of standard fishing spots}}

==Types of fish==
{{main|Fish}}
When a player catches a fish, it will be in raw form and cannot be eaten until it is cooked, indicated by name and colour. For example, when salmon is first caught, the item is called "[[raw salmon]]", but once cooked it turns darker red and its name changes to "[[salmon]]". (All items caught through the Fishing skill are referred to here as "fish", despite some being classified as crustaceans or other taxons.)

