==Minigames==
===Fishing Trawler===
{{Main|Fishing Trawler}}
Fishing Trawler is a fishing [[minigame]] run by [[Murphy]] that players can play at [[Port Khazard]]. Players need at least a minimum of level 15 fishing to participate. Players board a trawler boat and work as a team to prevent the boat from sinking as they are sailed for 12 minutes around the sea. It can be overwhelming for a single player, so it is recommended to bring friends, a clan, or other experienced fishers. Fishing Trawler was released 28 July 2003. Currently, world 116 is the RuneScape designated Trawler world. At the end of every trip, you get a load of fish and other assorted items (i.e. [[rusty sword]]s) the Fishing Trawler is the only event to give [[Raw tiger shark|tiger sharks]].

===Fish Flingers===
{{Main|Fish Flingers}}
Fish Flingers is a [[Distractions and Diversions|Distraction and Diversion]] released [[23 March]] 2010. Games are scheduled every 20 minutes and last for 10 minutes. [[Fisherman (Fish Flingers)|Fishermen]] stand in the most popular fishing spots all the time and can teleport players to the game location. For three minutes before the game starts, they will shout out periodically. Games are a solo, non-competitive minigame, although players frequently cooperate. Rewards are [[experience]], fish, and tackle boxes, as well as pieces of the [[Fishing Outfit]] which gives up to 5% bonus experience when fishing.

===Prifddinas Waterfall Fishing===
{{Main|Prifddinas Waterfall Fishing}}
From level 93 Fishing, players can start fishing for [[crystal urchin]]s in [[Prifddinas]] at the [[Prifddinas Waterfall]]. The area also requires level 90 [[Agility]], [[Ranged]], and [[Strength]], in order to use a [[mith grapple|mithril grapple]] to access the waterfall. There is a [[Hidey-holes (Grapple)|hidey-hole]] to allow infinite grapples.

